    "faqQ1": "How long does it take to develop a corporate mobile application?",
    "faqA1": "Timeline depends on scope and integrations. Streamlined operational apps (e.g., ordering or field checklists) are typically delivered in 4 to 8 weeks, while complex multi-module systems with dedicated administrative backends take between 8 to 16 weeks. A precise timeline is provided during discovery.",
    "faqQ2": "Will our application be published officially on Google Play?",
    "faqA2": "Yes. If your objective is public distribution, CONEXUS manages store configuration, graphic assets, privacy policies, and official submission to Google Play. For internal-only corporate tools, we configure private Managed Google Play distribution.",
    "faqQ3": "Can the app integrate with our existing ERP or CRM software?",
    "faqA3": "Yes. We build applications with API-first architectures (REST/JSON), enabling direct connections with ERPs (such as Totvs, SAP, Bling, Omie), existing databases, payment gateways, and WhatsApp messaging systems.",
    "faqQ4": "How do maintenance and updates work after launch?",
    "faqA4": "We provide continuous support plans ensuring your app remains fully operational, compliant with new Android and Google Play API guidelines, and ready for feature upgrades as your business evolves.",
    "faqQ5": "Can the application function offline without an internet connection?",
    "faqA5": "Yes. For fieldwork and mobile sales, we build encrypted local databases. Users carry out tasks normally, and data synchronizes automatically in the background once network connectivity is restored.",
